course: dictionary
lesson: 3373
title: Executor: the person who carries out a will
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A will is a legal paper that someone writes while they are alive. It says who gets their money, house and belongings after they die.
explain: The word «executor» is the person named in the will to make sure its wishes are carried out. «The person who carries it out is called the executor.» Think of an executor as the one who sorts things out after someone has died.
explain: The word also has a wider meaning: anyone who carries out a plan or task can be called an executor. The words around it give the clue. If you see will, died or money nearby, you are reading the law meaning.
fact: An executor is the person named in a will to carry out what it says.
fact: «Executor» means the person who carries out a will after someone has died, sharing out money and things.
fact: A will is a legal paper saying who gets your money, house and belongings after you die.
fact: In a more general sense, an executor is a person who carries out a plan or task.
fact: Context clues such as «will», «died» and «money» show you which meaning is being used.
exercise: «A will is a legal paper someone writes while alive, saying who gets their money, house and belongings after they die; the person who carries it out is called the executor.» What is an executor? | *The person named in a will to carry out what it says | A house left to a family | A person who writes a will while alive | A paper that says who gets the money
exercise: Grandad has died. His sister has been named in his will to share out his things. What is she? | A solicitor who writes wills for a living | A neighbour who keeps his keys | A cousin who lives far away | *An executor
exercise: Find and copy one word from «the person who carries it out is called the executor» that tells you the executor works with a will. | executor | called | *will | carries
test: In its wider sense, what can an executor be? | A large house on a hill | A kind of cake made with fruit | *A person who carries out a plan or task | A bird that lives near the sea
test: Mum says the executor is sorting out Grandad's things. Why is she called that? | Because she writes poetry | *Because the will named her to carry out its wishes | Because she lives in his house | Because she is very tall
exam: Which meaning fits executor when a will is read after someone dies? | Someone who writes a will while alive | A bank that holds money for children | *The person named in a will to carry out what it says | A legal paper saying who gets money
